# Mobile screen layout consistency

Tab roots and stack screens share one top chrome and one page-body gutter. Do not invent a
per-screen inset under the title bar.

## Top chrome

- Use **`HeaderBar`** for the slot under the status bar: safe-area inset and a 44pt row. No
  divider, hairline, or shadow under the title. The title is regular weight (`400`) at 17pt.
- Stack titles go through **`ThemedStackHeader`** (already wraps `HeaderBar` via
  **`HeaderBarChrome`**). Trailing header actions use **`HeaderBarAction`** in `headerRight` —
  do not invent a one-off top-right `Pressable`. When that slot has more than one action, wrap
  them in **`HeaderBarActions`**, which spaces siblings by `spacing.md`.
  **Share**, and **Boost** on screens that offer it, on podcast, album, artist, episode, and
  track detail, belong in the stack title-bar slot (`HeaderBarAction` in `headerRight`, wrapped
  in `HeaderBarActions` when there is more than one). **Checking all notifications** is the Home
  tab root only (`HomeRoot` with `headerBackChoice` `none`). `ThemedStackHeader` puts
  `HomeNotificationsBell` first in `headerRight` (`HeaderBarActions`), to the left of Home's
  overflow menu. testIDs `home-notifications-bell` and `home-notifications-bell-badge`. Browse,
  For Me, My Library, and More roots do not get this bell. A tab opened from More shows Back,
  so it does not get this bell. Pushed screens do not get it. The bell stays visible signed out
  and without notifications access. Press goes through `resolveNotificationsBellPress`, then
  `navigateToNotificationsInboxScreen()` or `openGate`. Signed out, that press calls
  `openGate('needs_account')`. Signed in with notifications access denied, it calls `openGate`
  with that reason. While `isTierKnown === false`, press opens the inbox. The inbox is root
  route `NotificationsInbox` with `ROOT_SLIDE_UP_SCREEN_OPTIONS`. The leading control is a down
  caret (testID `notifications-inbox-dismiss`, catalog `misc.dismiss`). Link path `notifications`
  (a link, push tap, or banner tap opens this route; signed out, that path opens the inbox login
  fill). The unread count is this bell's badge. **Search** is the Home tab root only, in
  `headerLeft` (`HomeSearchButton`, testID `home-search`). `navigateToSearchScreen()` raises
  root route `Search` with `ROOT_SLIDE_UP_SCREEN_OPTIONS`. The Search root leading control is a
  down caret (testID `search-dismiss`). Pages pushed on that stack keep a back chevron. It is
  not a bottom tab or a Tab Bar settings row. It stays visible signed out. Browse, For Me,
  My Library, and More roots do not show this control. When Home is opened from More, back
  occupies the leading slot. **Turning notifications on or off for a channel**
  is podcast, album, and artist detail only. Prop `notifications` on `ChannelHeader`, trailing
  on the action row, `layout="inline"`, `CHANNEL_HEADER_SETTINGS_ICON_SIZE`. testIDs
  `podcast-detail-notifications-toggle`, `album-detail-notifications-toggle`, and
  `artist-detail-notifications-toggle`. The bell stays visible when signed out.
  `useChannelNotifications` and the settings-pane switches stay. Do not put this bell in the
  stack title bar. Do not put it on episode, track, livestream, clip, or any other item screen.
  Add by RSS channel pages have no bell. **Channel settings** are a gear on the title row of
  `ChannelHeader` (podcast, album, and artist), top-aligned with the title. The glyph is
  **`CHANNEL_HEADER_SETTINGS_ICON_SIZE`** (22), one step under the stack-header icons. The title
  is at most two lines, then an ellipsis, and stops `spacing.md` short of the gear. Subscribe
  packs at the leading edge of the action row. The channel bell is the trailing edge of that
  same row, in line with the gear, and is not a node inside `actions`. The row sits on the
  bottom edge of the 78pt artwork, so a one-line title and a two-line title keep that row in
  place. A subtitle under the title shares that top group, and the title is then one line, so
  the action row still lands on the artwork edge. The gear stays visible when signed out. It is
  not a section chip and not a stack-title control. Pressing it shows the settings pane;
  pressing it again, or choosing a section chip, returns to that section. Do not place share in
  `ChannelHeader`. Do not add the inbox bell on a non-Home tab root, a pushed screen, or a tab
  opened from More. Web keeps its header row; see **about-summary-web-mobile-alignment**. Do not
  restyle that row, and do not remove `NotificationIconButton` from a page that mounts the
  parent channel header.
  `ChannelHeader` `actions` is the leading cluster of that bottom row. RSS and website stay on
  About. **Header icons and header action labels use `tokens.text.primary`** (same as the title) —
  never `tokens.text.accent` / link blue. That color lives in **`HeaderBarAction`**; do not
  reintroduce accent tint on back, overflow, or trailing header controls. Stack header action
  icons use that component's **26pt** default. The back glyph stays 28. Do not pass a smaller
  icon size on a stack header action. The channel gear is the smaller glyph. A header More opens
  **`MoreMenu`** — a bottom sheet that appears instantly: tertiary action group with centered
  bold rows, then a separate opaque quaternary Cancel block (same bold weight). Do not slide or
  fade, do not use a translucent Cancel fill, do not use a centered card, and do not style Cancel
  as a pill.
- Tab roots use the same title slot (Home, For Me, …). For Me is the Recommendations tab: the
  bar says For Me and the screen title says Recommendations. Signed in, Edit is a row in that
  screen's overflow menu, under List and Grid (testID `recommendations-edit`). It opens Taste
  Profile settings. Signed out, the row is omitted. A long title ellipsizes in the
  center column, with padding on both sides, so it does not cover the leading or trailing icons.
  Search is not a tab. Its field and chips sit in the body under the Search title, opened from
  the Home title bar's leading control.
  Page controls such as Home's media-type pills sit in the body under that bar, not inside it.

## Page body under the bar

The first content below `HeaderBar` uses **`screenBodyInsets(tokens.spacing)`** from
`apps/mobile/src/theme/screenLayout.ts`:

- **Top:** `spacing.lg` between the title row and the first body control
- **Horizontal:** `spacing.lg` on both sides of that body

`MobileScreenContainer` already applies this. Home's feed list and Search's field / chips / list
must use the same helper — not a one-off `padding` / `margin`, and not a second inner `Card`
padding on top of the page gutter.

Screen lists (Home, Search, Library, …) are unboxed: no perimeter `Card` around the rows. `Card`
is a surface for grouped settings or section chrome, not for a scrolling result list.

Internal gaps stay on the screen. Prefer one column **`gap`** for a stack of related controls so
spaces stay equal by construction (Search: field → chips → list rule all share `spacing.base`).
Gaps that belong together follow **even-content-spacing**. Loading
(`VerticalCenter`, `LoadingSection`) fills leftover height and stays centered. Empty and error
copy (`CallToActionSection`, `ListEmpty`, `ListError`) sits at the start of the content column,
under the chips, using the page gutter. It does not replace that gutter.

## Search field and chips

**`TextField`** owns the painted pill: tertiary fill, no resting outline, a 2px transparent
border that becomes `tokens.border.primary` on focus. Form fields pass **`eyebrow` + a
distinct `placeholder`** (web inset caption; taller pill) —
**form-eyebrow-placeholder**. **`SearchField`** and **`ListFilterField`** omit `eyebrow` and
stay compact. Search adds the leading magnifying glass and a search return key. Both paint an X
at the right edge of the pill while the value is non-empty. The X is icon-only. **`SearchField`**
names it with the shared Clear Search string. **`ListFilterField`** names it with the shared Clear
Filter string. Neither field takes a label prop for the X. Pressing it sets the value to an empty
string through the same change handler as typing, then focuses the field so the keyboard stays up.
It does not submit. Form **`TextField`**s omit it. Do not restyle a bare `TextInput` with a
perimeter stroke, and do not put a second label above an eyebrow field.

The pill stays the hit target. A tap on the padding, the empty space, or the leading glass
focuses the input. A tap on the X clears the value and leaves the field focused. `TextField`
implements both. Do not rebuild that per screen.
Do not enlarge the area by adding padding on the `TextInput` (that moves the placeholder).
Submit stays on the keyboard return key. Leaving the screen blurs the field — do not keep a
caret or focus ring across a tab switch. Focus again only when the user taps or a screen
explicitly requests it (`autoFocus`). The same contract applies to other painted controls you
touch: the visible shape is what the finger can press.

Two or three filters under a field use **`OptionChipGroup`**. Selected chip = `buttonPrimary` fill.
Settings density (2–3 chips vs option-list screen) is **mobile-settings-option-density**.

Standalone cover art uses **`CoverImage`** (`expo-image`, memory+disk cache). A stationary tap
opens the **`ImageViewer`** root screen (`buildRootSlideUpDismissOptions`): it slides up and
dismisses from a down chevron or a downward drag that starts in the header band (status inset +
44pt title row), on iOS and Android. The header control is a down chevron
(`HeaderBarChrome` `backIcon="chevron-down"`, `misc.dismiss`). `NotificationsInbox` is a root
screen on the same dismiss options, with the same down-chevron and header-band drag
(`notifications-inbox-dismiss`). Full player and Search root share that contract; Search pages
after the first route keep a back chevron and do not dismiss the card by drag. Pass
**`viewerUri`** from **`primaryLightboxArtworkUrl`** (or the channel variant) so the screen loads
the largest original, not the list thumb. Pass **`addByRssFeedUrl`** when the artwork belongs to
an Add by RSS feed. The route never carries an `Authorization` value; the screen resolves those
headers from the feed URL. Do not add a nested image tap when the parent row, cell, or header is
already the pressable control (`opensViewer={false}`). Resolve display `uri` with
**`primaryListArtworkUrl`** — see **header-hero-image-sources**. When navigating from a painted
row into a detail header, pass preview params so the same list URL paints on the first frame —
see **mobile-image-loading**. The app stays portrait; the viewer does not unlock landscape.

## Hub menus

More, Library, and Browse use **`MenuListScreen`**. A **`SectionHeading`** sits **above** its
`Card` (`typography.heading`, `tokens.text.accent` — same as channel Settings groups) with
`spacing.lg` before the card and `spacing.xl` between groups. In-content section labels use
accent so they read as structure against primary body copy; do not invent a second
section-heading color. A menu row passes **`spacing.lg`** vertical padding, and its subtitle
uses **`typography.body`**. Rows that push a screen show a `›`. In-place actions (Log out) set
`showsChevron: false`. Skip empty sections. More Account includes Login / Sign up or Log out.

## Settings cards

A label beside a switch is **`SettingsSwitchRow`**. The title is the menu title size (19), the
same size as a **`ListRow`** title, and a single-line title shifts so its ink lines up with the
switch. Do not put a raw `Text`, or a `ListRow` with a trailing switch, in that role.

Groups inside a settings card separate with a hairline (`StyleSheet.hairlineWidth` and the
border token). They are not wrapped in a bordered box. Space above that line equals space below
it (`spacing.lg`). The hairline has no extra horizontal inset: it runs the width of the card.
There is no line above the first group.

**`settingsCardGap`** (`spacing['2xl']`) is the space between settings cards.
**`settingsCardInnerGap`** (`spacing.lg`) is the column gap from a heading to its description to
its button. Apply it as `gap` so a missing description leaves no margin behind.

An option-list row matches a menu row: the same title size, **`spacing.lg`** vertical padding,
and a 26pt check (`LIST_ROW_ACTION_ICON_SIZE`).

## List rows

Media and result rows use **`HomeFeedRow`** (or **`ListRow`** when the layout is title/subtitle
only). A podcast, album, or artist row pads with
**`listRowVerticalPadding(LIST_ROW_SHOW_VERTICAL_INSET)`** (10) from
`apps/mobile/src/theme/screenLayout.ts`: the same inset above and below the artwork, which with
the 78pt mark is a 98pt row. Episode, clip, and track rows pad with
**`listRowVerticalPadding(tokens.spacing.lg)`**. The Downloads list and a category row use
**`spacing.base`**. **`ListRow`** defaults to **`spacing.base`**; a menu row passes
**`spacing.lg`**. Row artwork is **`LIST_ROW_ARTWORK_SIZE`** (78). Mini-player art is
**`MINI_PLAYER_ARTWORK_SIZE`** (60).

Stack every `HomeFeedRow` identity line — channel date, title, and footer, and item show name,
title, and date — with a column **`gap`** of **`spacing.xs`**. A podcast, album, or artist row
stays 98pt because the artwork inset sets the height, and those three lines sit inside the 78pt
mark. **`ListRow`** keeps **`spacing.sm`** between its title and subtitle. Do not use
`marginTop` / `marginBottom` on each line, so a missing line adds no leftover space.
The text stack uses `justifyContent: 'center'` so it stays vertically centered on the artwork.
The gap between artwork and text is **`listRowArtworkGap(tokens.spacing)`** (`spacing.base`) on
`HomeFeedRow` and `ListRow`, not a per-screen `spacing.md` or a leading `marginLeft`. The
channel header mark is also 78. Its art→title gap stays **`spacing.lg`**, the header's own
seam. The title row and the action row share that 78pt height.

A Home show row is the date, then the title, then "{count} downloaded", including zero. That
title is regular weight (`400`) at 19pt. Episode, clip, and track titles use the same weight
and size. A Browse podcast or album row is the date, then the title, then the author. Episode,
clip, and track rows stay show name, title, then date. Item
and channel pub dates use the same type: 14pt, weight 700, line height 20,
**`tokens.text.link`**. An item description under that identity is 14pt, weight 400, line
height 20, in secondary color. It sits **`listRowDescriptionGap`** (`spacing.base`) under the
identity block, the same width as the gap beside the artwork, so the paragraph keeps that
clearance when it wraps under the image. The play, duration, and progress band keeps its own
gap below that text. An Add by RSS show row
has the date and the title and no download count, and it does not reserve that line.

Home subscription markers stay on those shared row/cell components: list live is centered on
a channel row's artwork, the downloaded count is the line under the title, and unseen on a
channel row is a numberless `UnseenIndicator` in a slim full-height rail at the far right of
the row (dot centered on the whole row height). On a channel-detail item row the same
indicator sits at the trailing top of the title line. Grid is live top-right, unseen
bottom-right, downloaded bottom-left. A livestream item row states its status in the play
band, in the slot where an episode row shows its duration: the Live badge while on the air
and a neutral Scheduled or Ended badge otherwise. The badge replaces the duration. Only a
Live row has Play, with the badge beside it. A Scheduled or Ended row has no Play: the badge
starts the band and More sits at the far end. Pressing any livestream row opens its livestream
page. The date stays on the date line under the title, and the context line carries only the
show name. A livestream inside an album uses this same episode row, never the compact track
row. Channel rows keep Live on the artwork. See **mobile-reusable-components**.

A podcast, album, or artist row **never** shows the More ellipsis. Channel-level actions use
swipe-left (`SwipeActionRow`) and the matching grid long-press when that list has a remove
action. Search results are channel rows too on **mobile and web**: tap (or click) opens the
feed; no More menu. Mobile Search also has no swipe remove. The More ellipsis is for
playable content: episodes, clips, tracks, and livestreams. On an episode or clip row the
one-tap download sits in the action band, immediately left of More, and the title uses the
header width. On a track row, which has no play band, that control stays immediately left of
More in the identity row.

Icon-only controls share **`LIST_ROW_ACTION_SIZE`** (44) and bare glyphs use
**`LIST_ROW_ACTION_ICON_SIZE`** (26); Play’s triangle uses **`LIST_ROW_PLAY_ICON_SIZE`** (16)
inside the glowing `play` Button. Prefer Button `variant="play"` for the media-row Play circle and
`variant="ghost"` for bare More; Download/trash stay borderless at the same hit target.

Under a channel header, **`listHeaderStackGap(tokens.spacing)`** (`spacing.lg`) is the gap
**above** the chip row (header → chips). Do not mix `md` on one seam and `lg` on another for that
header stack.

## Stacked preview identity

A screen that stacks a large cover, a title, a byline, and a full description uses the helpers in
`apps/mobile/src/theme/screenLayout.ts`. Put each seam on that line as `marginTop`, so a missing
author or description adds no empty band. The scroll column around the identity block, the
explainer, and the action keeps `gap: spacing.lg`. Page padding stays **`screenBodyInsets`** plus
`paddingBottom: spacing.lg`.

| Name                            | Returns        | Seam                                                                    |
| ------------------------------- | -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `PREVIEW_IDENTITY_ARTWORK_EDGE` | `160`          | Cover edge. The style and `decodeEdge` share it.                       |
| `previewIdentityArtworkGap`     | `spacing.lg`   | Cover to title                                                          |
| `previewIdentityBylineGap`      | `spacing.base` | Title to author                                                         |
| `previewIdentityDescriptionGap` | `spacing.xl`   | Author to description, or title to description when there is no author |

Type on that stack: title **`typography.display`**, author **`typography.prose`** in secondary
color, description **`typography.prose`** in primary color. The directory explainer is
**`HelperNote`** with `scale="reading"` (`typography.body`, `HELPER_NOTE_READING_ICON_SIZE`).
Adding, error, and notice lines on that screen use **`typography.body`**.

Every `HomeFeedRow` identity stack uses a column `gap` of `spacing.xs`. **`ListRow`** title and
subtitle stay on `spacing.sm`. **`ChannelHeader`** stays the side-by-side header. The next
screen with this stack uses these helpers. Screens that already exist keep their current
spacing and type.

## Chip row → next block

Space **between** chips in a row is **`chipRowGap()`** (6).
**`SectionChip`** and **`MenuSelectChip`** apply it as `marginRight`. **`OptionChipGroup`**
applies it as the row `gap`.

A page action that shares a chip row (`ChipAction` inside **`ChipRowWithActions`**) is always a
band above the chips on mobile — Add Feed and Check for Updates on Add by RSS. The action group
wraps on its own line (`chipRowGap()`), start-aligned. Web keeps the wrap-to-the-right behavior
in `@podverse/ui` `ChipRowWithActions`. Recommendations Edit is an overflow-menu row, not a
chip-row action.

Space **below** chips that sit above a list is **`listChipRowBottomGap(tokens.spacing)`**
(`spacing.base`, the same value as `listFilterContentGap`). **`SectionChipRow`** applies it as
the row's own `paddingBottom`. An **`OptionChipGroup`** placed above a list (Queue, History,
Search) gets that same `paddingBottom` on the header that holds the chips. Do **not** add a
second `paddingBottom` / `marginTop` on a screen that already uses `SectionChipRow` (Home/Browse
`selectorSection`, podcast filter `marginTop`, About surface `marginTop`) or the seam doubles or
disappears when the next sibling changes. Form chips inside a card stay on form spacing.

Whatever follows the chips (filter field, episode list, about prose, podroll) inherits that same
gap. A filter between the chips and the hairline then has equal space above the field and below
it. Filter fields use **`listFilterFieldBottomMargin`** for the filter→row seam only.

## Filter field → content seam

The gap from a **`ListFilterField`** bottom edge to the first list row or grid tile is
**`listFilterContentGap(tokens.spacing)`** (`spacing.base`). Wrap the field in
**`ListFilterHeader`** and put **`listFilterFieldBottomMargin(tokens.spacing, nextContentTopPadding)`**
on that wrapper's `style` (`marginBottom`):

- **List** rows that use `listRowVerticalPadding(spacing.base)`: pass `spacing.base` so the field
  does not double the row's top padding.
- **Grid** tiles with no top padding: pass `0`.

`ListFilterHeader` does not paint a line. When **`hasItemsBelow`** is true, its `paddingBottom`
is `listFilterContentGap` so the field does not sit on the first row. Pass that when the list
has at least one row or tile after the field. Omit it when the list is empty or the term hid
every row. Do not put that padding on the field itself.

Do not use a raw `marginBottom: spacing.md` on the filter (too tight on grid once list padding is
added elsewhere, too loose on list when stacked with row padding). Home switches the second
argument with `isGridView` so both view modes share one seam.

Content rows (`HomeFeedRow` and the same catalog: playlist, profile, chapter, category,
download, artist albums, and podroll on artist, album, and podcast) draw one top hairline
(`StyleSheet.hairlineWidth` + `themeStyles.border.borderColor`), including the first row. There
is no bottom hairline, so the last row does not leave a line on the list edge. An empty list has
no row and no line. Grid tiles have no row hairline, so nothing draws a line above a grid.
Settings cards do not use this top hairline.

Do not place a standalone divider under chips, under a filter, or between chips and the list.
Search, Queue, and History do not render a `listRule`. The first row's top border is the only
line, and only when that row exists.

Settings and menu cards keep their own separators (a line between rows after the first, or under
an in-card header). Do not give the first row inside those cards a top hairline.
`ReorderableSections` default rows follow that card rule (bottom hairline, omitted on the last
row). Content lists that wrap `HomeFeedRow` use `rowContainerVariant="plain"`. A single
`HomeFeedRow` embedded in a bordered card (clip detail) also omits the hairline; the card border
is the edge.

## Fill empty lists do not scroll

When a list's only body is a fill info state (`LoadingSection` / `CallToActionSection` /
**`ListEmpty`** as `ListEmptyComponent`), there is nothing to scroll. Use **`FillList`** instead
of raw `FlatList` — it locks bounce, over-scroll, pull-to-refresh, and `scrollEnabled` whenever
`data` is empty and `ListEmptyComponent` is set.

**`ListEmpty`** sits at the start of the list body. Its sentence is **`EmptyStateText`**: 24pt
light type on the glow fill, the same banner as a web empty list. **`CallToActionSection`** uses
that banner for its message, with the actions under it. The chip row's bottom gap is the space
above the banner. Do not center it in the leftover height.

Buttons in that fill (`CallToActionSection`, a `ListEmpty` action, `ListError` retry) are **full
width** of the fill column. Do not hug the label. Loading stays centered in `VerticalCenter`.

Podcast section lists use **`PodcastSectionList`**, which already composes **`FillList`** +
**`ListEmpty`**.

## Podcast detail pinned chrome

**`ChannelHeader`** and the section chip row stay **outside** the section list so they remain
visible while the rows scroll. **`ListFilterField`** stays in that list's `ListHeaderComponent` —
it is not pinned. Pull-to-refresh belongs on **`PodcastSectionList`** (the list below the chips),
so the spinner appears above the filter. Share and Boost stay in the stack `headerRight`.
The channel notification bell is the trailing control on `ChannelHeader`'s action row. Channel
settings are the gear at the top right of `ChannelHeader`.

## Podcast detail filter visibility

Show **`ListFilterField`** only when **`isFilterableSection(section)`** is true
(`podcastSections.ts`). Clips and podroll are **not** filterable — clips are server-paginated, and
podroll is a short publisher list without title filtering. Episodes, official soundbites, and
**Downloaded** are filterable.

**Downloaded** is always offered (with Episodes, About, and Clips): it lists finished offline
episodes for this channel from `downloadsRepository.listCompleteByChannel`. An empty list is a
real answer. Evidence chips (Official Clips, Podroll, …) sit **after** that always-on set so a
first-visit insert is at the end of the row — **mobile-section-chrome-cache**. While **Offline
Mode** is on, podcast detail opens on Downloaded — **mobile-offline-mode**. The section chip is
visit-local; every open starts on Episodes (or Downloaded while Offline Mode is on).

Sort and category controls sit in the chip-row **trailing** slot and use **filter** chrome (square
radius, accent outline) so they read as list narrows, not as sibling section pills. Mount them
**only when the current chip can use them** — `isSortableSection` / `isHomeSortableMediaType` /
`shouldShowBrowseSortChip` for sort, `shouldShowBrowseCategoryChip` for Categories. Unmount when
the filter cannot sort or pick a category (About, Podroll, Official Clips, music Browse types,
the category picker). Do not leave a disabled sort chip in the row to hold layout.

Section and media-type chips keep the order the caller handed in. Selecting one does not move it
to the front. Evidence chips resolve before Funding. People, when present, is the last content
chip. A first-visit insert stays at the end of that set, still before the optional sort / category
trailing chip. Channel settings are not a chip. A settings row that needs an account opens the
login gate on press.

## Action error icons

An error glyph, or a failed download row that has no glyph, does not retry or toast on its own.
The next press opens `ConfirmDialog` through `useActionError` (`openPlaybackError` /
`openDownloadError`): a kind-specific explanation, a reportable detail line when one exists,
Cancel, and a retry action. The dialog does not open until that press. List-row play buttons stay
play/pause; pre-play `noticeKey` text stays inline.

## Action-gated account / membership

When the screen is usable and one control is gated, keep the control visible. On press, call
`useMembershipGate().openGate(reason)` so `ConfirmDialog` explains the denial. `needs_account`
confirms to Login; membership reasons confirm to the Membership screen. Copy comes from
`membershipGateCopy` (exhaustive on `AccessDenialReason`). Do not park an inline
"Account required" card (`GatedFeatureNotice`) above a button the user has not tapped.

The exception is a **fill empty**: the whole body is missing because the feature requires an
account (Library history, playlists). That still uses **`CallToActionSection`** below.

Helper copy that is not the content itself (directory explainer, why-add notes) uses
**`HelperNote`** — tertiary fill and a leading info icon, centered on the sentence. The default
scale is `compact` (caption type, `HELPER_NOTE_ICON_SIZE`). A stacked preview passes
`scale="reading"`.

## Login-gated fill states

When a screen's body is empty because the feature requires an account, use **`CallToActionSection`**
plus a Login action — not a bare `ListEmpty`. Prefer
**`AuthAwareLoadState`** with `showAuthRequired` (it defaults to `authentication.login_required`);
otherwise wire `CallToActionSection` as the `FillList` empty (or the only `MobileScreenContainer`
child).

The body is the generic login-required sentence — see **generic-login-required-copy**. Hide the
in-body heading on that fill — the `HeaderBar` title is enough.

## Static form-style screens (body + CTAs)

Consent prompts, login / sign-up, and other **static** screens (prose or fields, then a decision)
are not lists. Do not use one column `gap` for both the body and the buttons — that makes the
first CTA look like another paragraph.

- **Body** (copy, dates, fields) keeps a tight internal gap (`spacing.md` or `spacing.base`).
- Choice chips on a form use **`FormField`**. The label names the field and must not repeat an
  option. It sits `spacing.md` above `OptionChipGroup` or a locked value.
- **Actions** use **`FormActions`**, a column in its own block. Every action is full width.
  Array order is top to bottom. On a page, sheet, or consent prompt the way out sits above the
  action that continues: Reject above Accept, Cancel above Save. The continuing button is the
  last one, where the thumb rests after reading. `ConfirmDialog` is the exception: confirm then
  cancel, so a slip toward the bottom does not commit. A destructive action stays its own
  `FormActions` under the column, with `formActionsGap` above it. Do not share the body's `gap`
  with the action block.
- Text a person reads on a page, sheet, or form is **`typography.prose`** (17 / 24). That
  includes legal and about copy. `CopyMarkdown` uses the same role for paragraphs and lists.
  Do not hardcode `fontSize`. A `Text` with no size is the platform 14 and is not a shipped
  reading size. The agreement date is not its own prose line: it is a caption under the
  accordion title.
- A checkbox label beside that copy is **`typography.body`** (15 / 21), one step under the
  paragraph. The control is not a second block of reading text.
- Help, a warning, and a feed status line such as "Last Parsed" use **`typography.body`**
  (15 / 21). A menu-row subtitle uses body too. **`caption`** stays for a count, or for the
  agreement date under an accordion title. The Terms of Service "Valid since" line is
  **`typography.heading`** in **`tokens.text.link`**.
- **`proseDisclosureGap`** (`spacing.lg`) is the extra margin above a disclosure that follows
  prose. The last paragraph already has `spacing.lg` below it, so the seam opens to
  `spacing['4xl']`. Do not put `formActionsTopGap` on that card; it stacks on the paragraph
  margin.
- **`formActionsTopGap`** (`spacing['4xl']`) is the seam above an agreement checkbox and the
  action column, and between those two. Those seams are equal, and they match the prose-to-
  disclosure seam once the paragraph margin is counted. Do not reuse the body's `spacing.md` /
  `spacing.base` gap for the decision seams.
- **`formActionsGap`** (`spacing.lg`) is the gap between the buttons inside the action column.
  Helpers live in `screenLayout.ts`.
- Form, dialog, checkout, and other page or section call-to-action buttons use **`Button`
  `size="form"`** (`FORM_BUTTON_MIN_HEIGHT`, 52pt, 17pt semibold) and are full width.
  `FormActions` applies that size. A raw `Button` that is the decision on that block does too:
  membership purchase, add, import and export, account actions, and check-feed. 44pt is the tap
  floor; an eyebrow field is about 66pt. 52pt sits between them so the label is easy to read and
  the control is easy to hit. Header, row, banner, and identity-block actions (Subscribe, Share,
  Play) stay `sm` or the default `md`. Fill empties (`CallToActionSection`, `ListEmpty`,
  `ListError`) stay `lg`.
- Do not hug a form button to its label.
- Do not add a second display heading when the stack title already names the screen.
- Full-screen Modal variants also use **`ModalSafeArea`**.

Login and Sign up already use this seam above Submit. The Taste Profile consent prompt
(`TasteProfileAgreementBody`) uses the same helpers for Yes / No / How It Works. Under
`AgreementChoices`, `proseDisclosureGap` sits above the disclosure and `formActionsTopGap` starts
under it: accordion to the "I have read" checkbox, then checkbox to the action block. A prompt
with no checkbox uses that same seam from the accordion to the action column.

## Login / Sign up overlay

Login and Sign up slide up as a full-screen `Modal` over the tab shell — they must not replace
the navigator. Dismiss with a down chevron (`HeaderBarChrome` `backIcon="chevron-down"`,
`testID="auth-dismiss"`) or a downward drag that starts in the header band, on iOS and Android.
A drag close skips the Modal's slide so the finger motion is the only exit. Forgot Password keeps
a back chevron and does not dismiss by drag. Do not add a Cancel button. The account switch is
body text plus a link-style `Pressable` under Submit (`auth-switch-signup` /
`auth-switch-login`). Fields use **`TextField`** with an inset **`eyebrow`** and a **distinct**
**`placeholder`** (example or hint — never the same string as the eyebrow; see
**form-eyebrow-placeholder**). Confirm-password keeps a password-hint placeholder while its
eyebrow stays `Confirm password`. Submit uses **`FormActions`**.

A successful sign-up replaces the form with its own screen: header title, one sentence to check
email (`signup-success-message`), and a Login button (`signup-success-login`) so someone who
verifies on the web can open login from here. On the form, the agreement date is a caption under
the terms accordion title. The "I have read" checkbox sits under that accordion, above Create
Account, with `formActionsTopGap` on each of those seams.

## Full-screen Modal safe area

A React Native `Modal` is a new native window. Insets from the app-root `SafeAreaProvider` do
not apply inside it, so a bare `SafeAreaView` reports 0 and content sits under the status bar.
Wrap Modal bodies in **`ModalSafeArea`** (`components/screen/ModalSafeArea`), which remounts
`SafeAreaProvider` and insets all four edges. The auth sheet already remounts the provider for
the same reason. Do not rely on the root provider alone for full-screen Modals.

## Do not

- Use a different page gutter (`md`, `2xl`, raw numbers) for the body under `HeaderBar`.
- Rebuild the title-bar height or type in a screen-local `StyleSheet`.
- Add a divider, hairline, or shadow under `HeaderBar`.
- Put a second in-body display heading on a screen that already has a `HeaderBar` title.
- Use raw `FlatList` for a screen list that shows a fill empty or a centered loading state, then
  hand-toggle `scrollEnabled` / `bounces` at the screen.
- Add a standalone divider under chips or a filter. A podcast, album, or artist row uses
  `LIST_ROW_SHOW_VERTICAL_INSET`, not `spacing.lg` or `spacing.md`.
- Do not add a Notifications tab, a More row that opens the inbox, or an inbox bell on a
  non-Home tab root, a pushed screen, or a tab opened from More.
- Do not add a Search tab, a More row that opens Search, or a search control on a non-Home tab
  root, a pushed screen, or a tab opened from More.
- Do not put the channel on/off bell in a stack title bar, on an item screen, or inside
  `ChannelHeader` `actions`.

